A||N||4||BigTurbo87GT||Northstar w/ 5Speed  /Clutch travel question||||1||
Z||000000||BigTurbo87GT||09-25-2001||11:56 AM||||Hi guys, I have a simple question regarding the clutch arm range of motion (the arm the slave cylinder pushes against when disengaging clutch). The water/egr crossover on the back of the motor prevents the arm from making what seems to be a full range of motion, can I simply pull the arm off the shaft and rotate it so that it contacts the slave cylinder plunger sooner? This seems easy and plausible, the concern I would think is getting the correct range of motion so that I don't overdrive the clutch arm (if that's possible) or under drive it (clutch doesn't fully disengage).<BR>Maybe a more pertinent question would be, what is the required travel to fully disengage the clutch?<BR>Thanks for any input or guidance.<BR><P>------------------<BR>87 GT, Clean near stocker<BR>01 IS300||||reg||1
Z||000001||lowCG||09-25-2001||09:31 PM||||About 7/8";an inch will work,but I wouldn't go more than this.Any less and it won't work so good either.<BR>There are two different sizes of slave cyl. bore,I have the smaller of the two which gives an inch of throw with slightly more effort.||||reg||1
Z||000002||88formula||09-25-2001||09:40 PM||||BigTurbo87GT I tried to do that to my 5-speed clutch fork arm when I had trouble with my clutch. It will only go on one way because there are cogs on it that align it one way only and the bolt fits into a recess in the arm. The blot holding on the arm acts like a keyway also aligning the arm with the clutch fork.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||09-25-2001||11:24 PM||||Approximately 7/8" of travel is all that's needed, no interfearance here. (northstar with Getrag 5-speed ;)<P>Fortunately, when the clutch is NEWest, the travel will be as far towards teh coolant tube as it will ever be, as the clutch wears, the travel range will slowly move backwards (self-ajustment is cool :)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||BigTurbo87GT||09-26-2001||08:34 AM||||Thanks Guys, it's nice to have one less thing to worry about!||||reg||1
